{"availability":"available","full":"c4punks/CWIST","name":"CWIST","description":"A high-performance C17 web framework supporting HTTP/3, WebTransport, and PQC.","category":"Developer tools","language":"C","stars":17,"forks":7,"created":"2026-01-07T12:06:07Z","updated":"2026-10-11T05:48:55Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://c4punks.github.io/CWIST/","topics":["boringssl","c","grpc","http2","http3","http3-server","io-uring","lightweight","low-level","openssl","post-quantum-cryptography","quic","redis","systems-programming","tls13","web-development","web-framework","websocket","webtransport"],"demo":"https://c4punks.github.io/CWIST/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:18.141Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:18.141Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:18.141Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T07:26:18.141Z","stars":17,"forks":7}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["CWIST is a C17 web framework and application server with built-in HTTP/1.1, HTTP/2, HTTP/3 (QUIC), WebSocket, and WebTransport support, hybrid post-quantum TLS (X25519MLKEM768), an embedded SQLite ORM, and a synchronous iouring/epoll/kqueue reactor. It is written in plain C and links statically.","The benchmark results above demonstrate the advantages in latency, memory footprint, and determinism:"],"features":["Latency & Throughput. Under 400 concurrency (wrk -t12 -c400, CI run above), both CWIST paths deliver lower average latency and higher throughput than the Axum, Gin, and Spring Boot rows of the same run; the tuned…","Memory Efficiency. CWIST's resident footprint is a fraction of the Go row and orders of magnitude below the JVM row of the same CI run. In high-density container environments, this significantly reduces memory…","Tail Latency & Predictability. Zero-copy framing, thread-pinned worker execution, and generational arena allocators minimize latency variance and GC pauses.","Zero-Overhead FFI. Production libraries in finance, game servers, machine learning, and systems software written in C/C++ link directly into CWIST with zero FFI conversion or runtime bridge penalty.","Instant Cold Start. With no runtime VM warmup or GC initialization required, CWIST starts in milliseconds and immediately serves requests at full capacity."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/c4punks/CWIST/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"157dd562e75de1cd55e15210f385044a62afae4b9ed06bc1f8780ad50e10b135","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:18.254Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:18.254Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"CWIST is a C17 web framework and application server with built-in HTTP/1.1, HTTP/2, HTTP/3 (QUIC), WebSocket, and WebTransport support, hybrid post-quantum TLS (X25519MLKEM768), an embedded SQLite ORM, and a synchronous iouring/epoll/kqueue reactor. It is written in plain C and links statically.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/c4punks/CWIST/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"157dd562e75de1cd55e15210f385044a62afae4b9ed06bc1f8780ad50e10b135","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/c4punks/CWIST/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:18.255Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-11T05:48:55Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/c4punks/CWIST/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:18.257Z","hash":"157dd562e75de1cd55e15210f385044a62afae4b9ed06bc1f8780ad50e10b135","originalBytes":31888,"storedBytes":31888,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["cwist","app","http","server","docs","reactor","example","c1m","connection","tls","req","https","thread","classic","latency","path","rss","webtransport","config","connections","default","every","install","mode","one","per","pool","request","tutorials","cfg","client","each","environment","hello","kib","benchmark","cpu","file","get","p99","p99.999","port","threads","true","under","web","csw","epoll","held","notice.md","open","p90","spring","void","w